; KEY STRUCTURAL RULES (learned from reading p2pp/mcf.py + gcode.py):
;
;  1. Use G1 for travel moves, NOT G0.
;     P2PP only sets MOVEMENT bits for G1 commands.  G0 has MOVEMENT=0
;     and never updates backpass_line, so the first-pass back-classification
;     sweep triggered by ; CP TOOLCHANGE START would rewind all the way to
;     index -1 and reclassify the entire file as CLS_TOOL_START.
;
;  2. T{n} goes BETWEEN ; CP TOOLCHANGE UNLOAD and ; CP TOOLCHANGE LOAD.
;     PrusaSlicer emits the tool-change command here.  If T1 appears after
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE END, the block stays CLS_TOOL_PURGE for the entire
;     layer-1 print body, which counts that extrusion twice in the wrong
;     splice slot.
;
;  3. A G1 X Y travel move is required immediately after ; CP TOOLCHANGE END.
;     CLS_ENDPURGE only transitions to CLS_NORMAL when a non-tower XY G1
;     move is encountered (first-pass check at mcf.py line ~417).  Without
;     it, layer-1 print moves stay CLS_TOOL_PURGE and are mis-classified.
;
;  4. Set EXTRAENDFILAMENT=0 for predictable splice positions.
;     P2PP defaults extra_runout_filament=150 (variables.py:173).  This is
;     added to the final splice position via gcode_process_toolchange(-1) at
;     mcf.py:102.  Without EXTRAENDFILAMENT=0 the last splice is 150 mm
;     longer than the sum of all extruded lengths + splice offset.
;
; EXPECTED P2PP OUTPUT (SPLICEOFFSET=100, EXTRAENDFILAMENT=0, extrusion_multiplier=1.0):
;
;   First pass block classification:
;     Layer-0 print G1 X E       → CLS_NORMAL  (extrusion counted)
;     G1 X160 Y70 before TC      → CLS_TOOL_START (back-classified)
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE START      → CLS_TOOL_START
;     G1 X162 Y72 approach       → CLS_TOOL_START → comment, not counted
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE UNLOAD     → CLS_TOOL_UNLOAD
;     G1 E-0.8 retract           → CLS_TOOL_UNLOAD → comment, not counted
;     T1                         → CLS_TOOL_PURGE (T sets it), then back-
;                                   classified to CLS_TOOL_UNLOAD by LOAD
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE LOAD       → CLS_TOOL_UNLOAD (back-classifies T1)
;     G1 E0.8 prime              → CLS_TOOL_UNLOAD → comment, not counted
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE WIPE       → CLS_TOOL_PURGE
;     G1 X160 Y90 E10 wipe       → CLS_TOOL_PURGE  (extrusion counted)
;     ; CP TOOLCHANGE END        → CLS_ENDPURGE
;     G1 X10 Y10 (first move)    → CLS_ENDPURGE → reclassified CLS_NORMAL
;     Layer-1 print G1 X E       → CLS_NORMAL  (extrusion counted)
;
;   Second pass splice calculation:
;     T0:  gcode_process_toolchange(0); current_tool=-1 → no splice, sets current_tool=0
;     Layer-0 extrudes 5×30 mm   =  150.000 mm  total_material_extruded
;     T1:  gcode_process_toolchange(1):
;            location = 150.000 + 100 = 250.000 mm
;            splice 1 → { position: 250.000, length: 250.000, tool: 0 }
;     Wipe extrudes 1×10 mm      =   10.000 mm  (credited to T1)
;     Layer-1 extrudes 5×30 mm   =  150.000 mm  total = 310.000 mm
;     End:  gcode_process_toolchange(-1):
;            location = 310.000 + 100 + 0 (EXTRAENDFILAMENT) = 410.000 mm
;            splice 2 → { position: 410.000, length: 160.000, tool: 1 }
